w('README.md', "# YL - Yankee Language\n\nEsoteric programming language on PHP with unicode syntax.\n\n## Example\n\n```yl\n~CLS~ Point ~O~\n    ~MET~ init(x, y) ~O~ this.x = x; this.y = y ~C~\n    ~MET~ length() ~O~ ^ sqrt(this.x * this.x + this.y * this.y) ~C~\n~C~\n\n~DECL~ p = ~NEW~ Point(3, 4)\n~PR~ \"Length:\", p.length()\n```\n\n## Features\n\n- Unique unicode syntax (~DECL~ ~FN~ ~LAM~ ~O~ ~C~ ~CLS~ ~MET~ ~NEW~)\n- Gradual typing: ~DECL~ x :int = 5\n- OOP with ~INH~ inheritance: ~CLS~ Child ~INH~ Parent\n- Closures: ~LAM~ (x) ~O~ ^ x * 2 ~C~\n- Generators on PHP Fibers: ~YLD~ + ~EACH~\n- Async: ~ASY~ ~FN~, ~AWT~\n- Stdlib: prelude, math, list, string, json, datetime, http\n- REPL v4 with :vars, :load, multiline\n- Compiler YL->PHP (ylc.php)\n- Package manager (ylpkg.php)\n- Browser playground (playground/)\n\n## Quick start\n\n```bash\nphp yl.php examples/main.yl\n```\n\n## Docs (i18n)\n\n- Russian: /\n- English: /en/\n- Simplified Chinese: /zh-Hans/\n- Traditional Chinese (Taiwan style): /zh-Hant/\n\n## License\n\nMIT\n");

